  "articleBody": "Ugh, you've spent hours on that trim, only to step back and see gaps or uneven lines. It’s a common frustration, and usually, it comes down to a few key mistakes. First off, rushing your measurements is a huge no-no. Even a slight miscalculation means your pieces won't meet perfectly, especially at corners. Speaking of corners, assuming they're all perfectly 45 degrees is another trap. Walls and corners are rarely as square as you think, so test-fitting those miter joints is super important. Skipping glue at mitered joints is also a big one – that glue adds durability and helps prevent those corners from opening up over time. And then there's the fasteners: using nails too close to the edge of the board can cause splitting or visible imperfections. Finally, failing to keep a consistent reveal or overhang is a dead giveaway of a DIY job versus a professional one. You want those lines to be consistent! If you're wrestling with these issues, or have really irregular walls, sometimes it's best to bring in someone with the tools and experience. HH Remodeling LLC has been tackling detailed interior finish work since 2017 in places like Lakewood and Boulder, and we can help make your trim look fantastic.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}